  <text id="title" x="58" y="40" width="980" height="46" font="heading" size="30" color="ink" wrap="false">FCT title continuity depends on visible legal progression</text>
  <text id="subtitle" x="58" y="86" width="1094" height="30" font="body" size="16" color="muted">The platform connects application intake, verification, statutory title review, approval handoffs, signing, and registration so mass-housing and regularisation workflows do not disappear into manual opacity.</text>

  <shape id="step1" type="rect" x="74" y="172" width="166" height="126" fill="#ECFDF5" stroke="#BBF7D0" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="step1t" x="92" y="190" width="130" height="86" font="body" size="17" color="ink" align="center" anchor="middle"><p><strong>Intake</strong></p><p>Application, parcel match, and title-file readiness</p></text>
  <shape id="a1" type="arrow" x="248" y="223" width="46" height="24" fill="accent" head-ratio="0.34"/>

  <shape id="step2" type="rect" x="304" y="172" width="166" height="126" fill="#EFF6FF" stroke="#BFDBFE" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="step2t" x="322" y="190" width="130" height="86" font="body" size="17" color="ink" align="center" anchor="middle"><p><strong>Verification</strong></p><p>Document checks, issue flags, and legal completeness review</p></text>
  <shape id="a2" type="arrow" x="478" y="223" width="46" height="24" fill="accent" head-ratio="0.34"/>

  <shape id="step3" type="rect" x="534" y="172" width="166" height="126" fill="#ECFDF5" stroke="#BBF7D0" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="step3t" x="552" y="190" width="130" height="86" font="body" size="17" color="ink" align="center" anchor="middle"><p><strong>Regularisation</strong></p><p>Area-council, mass-housing, or statutory title alignment</p></text>
  <shape id="a3" type="arrow" x="708" y="223" width="46" height="24" fill="accent" head-ratio="0.34"/>

  <shape id="step4" type="rect" x="764" y="172" width="166" height="126" fill="#EFF6FF" stroke="#BFDBFE" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="step4t" x="782" y="190" width="130" height="86" font="body" size="17" color="ink" align="center" anchor="middle"><p><strong>Approval</strong></p><p>Desk escalation, supervisory review, and timed handoff control</p></text>
  <shape id="a4" type="arrow" x="938" y="223" width="46" height="24" fill="accent" head-ratio="0.34"/>

  <shape id="step5" type="rect" x="994" y="172" width="166" height="126" fill="#ECFDF5" stroke="#BBF7D0" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="step5t" x="1012" y="190" width="130" height="86" font="body" size="17" color="ink" align="center" anchor="middle"><p><strong>Signing</strong></p><p>Title completion, signed audit package, and custody trace</p></text>
  <shape id="a5" type="arrow" x="1146" y="315" width="0" height="54" fill="accent" rotation="90" head-ratio="0.34"/>

  <shape id="step6" type="rect" x="994" y="350" width="166" height="108" fill="#FEFCE8" stroke="#FDE68A" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="step6t" x="1012" y="366" width="130" height="76" font="body" size="17" color="ink" align="center" anchor="middle"><p><strong>Registration</strong></p><p>Official record visibility and post-title continuity</p></text>

  <shape id="value-card-1" type="rect" x="74" y="476" width="536" height="132" fill="surface" stroke="border" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="value-card-1t" x="98" y="500" width="488" height="84" font="body" size="18" color="ink" line-height="1.32"><p><strong color="brand">Public-service value</strong></p><p space-before="10">FCT leadership can see where title workflows are waiting, where verification breaks down, and how regularisation work is actually progressing across desks.</p></text>

  <shape id="value-card-2" type="rect" x="636" y="476" width="524" height="132" fill="surface" stroke="border" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="value-card-2t" x="660" y="500" width="476" height="84" font="body" size="18" color="ink" line-height="1.32"><p><strong color="brand">Oversight value</strong></p><p space-before="10">A visible progression path strengthens confidence in statutory title decisions, mass-housing issuance, and the integrity of records that matter to citizens and investors.</p></text>

